{# IN·08 — the month's mix by kind of incident, as a share of the whole.

   The same four hues the map paints an incident with, read here as arcs of one
   ring: the donut, the legend and the map are one palette, so a colour means the
   same thing wherever it is drawn. Biggest share first; a kind with nothing filed
   this month is left out rather than drawn as a zero arc
   ({@see IncidentDashboard::categoryShares}).

   The drawing is the chart layer's ({@see _charts.html.twig}); this partial turns
   the shares into labelled segments and centres the month's total. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiIncident/dashboard/_charts.html.twig' as charts %}
{% set shares = dashboard.categoryShares %}
<div class="c chartcard" data-w="bycat">
    <span class="tab">By category<span class="src">{% if dashboard.filter.from %}· {{ dashboard.filter.from|date('F Y')|lower }} {% endif %}· {{ dashboard.filedCount }} filed</span></span>
    {% set segments = [] %}
    {% for share in shares %}
        {% set segments = segments|merge([{
            label: share.category.label,
            class: share.category.colourKey,
            count: share.count,
        }]) %}
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="ch-donut">
        {{ charts.donut(segments, dashboard.filedCount) }}
    </div>
</div>
